# Kōlea — local secrets.
#
# `bun run setup` writes a `.dev.vars` for you, holding three random local
# secrets: MCP_PATH_SECRET, MEMBER_SESSION_SECRET and AI_KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET.
# Copy any other line you need from here into it, then restart `bun run dev`
# (wrangler reads the file once, at startup).
#
# Everything here is a secret. `.dev.vars` is gitignored, this example file is
# not, so never paste a real value below.
#
# All of it is optional. With no `.dev.vars` at all, Kōlea runs in console mode
# with MCP and Stripe switched off, and mails nobody.
#
# In production these go in Cloudflare, not here:
#   bunx wrangler secret put NAME --env production

# ── Mail ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave EMAIL_PROVIDER=console (the default in wrangler.jsonc) to keep everything
# in the in-app Outbox instead of sending for real.
EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Point Resend's webhook at /webhooks/resend. Without it, bounces and complaints
# never suppress, and your sending reputation degrades silently.
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxxxxxxxxx

# The one address a "send preview" may ever reach. Defaults to FROM_EMAIL,
# which is your own mailbox by definition.
PREVIEW_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Your mailing address, printed in the footer of broadcasts and sequence mail.
# Bulk mail law in most places asks for one. Unset, the line is left out.
# POSTAL_ADDRESS="1 Example Road, Springfield"

# ── Mailgun (instead of Resend) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=mailgun
# MAILGUN_API_KEY=key-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# The sending domain registered in Mailgun, and the region of the account.
# MAILGUN_DOMAIN=mg.example.com
# MAILGUN_REGION=us
# "HTTP webhook signing key" on Mailgun's Webhooks page, not the API key. Point
# Mailgun's webhooks at /webhooks/mailgun. Without it that endpoint answers 503
# and Mailgun retries, so bounces wait for the key instead of being lost.
# MAILGUN_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Sending domains ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. A Cloudflare API token with Zone:Read and DNS:Edit on the zones you
# send from. It adds an "Add to Cloudflare" button to the Sending domains
# screen. Unset, the records are shown to copy by hand.
# CLOUDFLARE_DNS_API_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Optional, local only: try that screen with no network and no token. The
# check reads an in-memory DNS, and the button writes to it.
# DNS_RESOLVER=fake
# CLOUDFLARE_DNS=fake

# ── Members on the public site ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the cookie a reader gets when they sign in by emailed link. Any long
# random string: openssl rand -hex 32. Unset, readers cannot sign in, and
# members-only and Premium posts show their teaser to everyone. Changing it
# signs every member out. `bun run setup` writes one for you.
# MEMBER_SESSION_SECRET=

# ── MCP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The unguessable path segment the MCP server answers on: POST /mcp/<secret>.
# Unset means the endpoint 404s, so MCP is off until you set this.
# Generate one: openssl rand -hex 24
MCP_PATH_SECRET=set-me-to-something-random

# ── Stripe ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Restricted key, read-only on charges / refunds / customers / products / prices.
# Used by the daily reconciliation cron and the stripe_* MCP tools.
# To sell from offer pages or run Premium memberships, the key must also be
# allowed to write Checkout Sessions. A read-only key cannot start a checkout.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=rk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# From the Stripe dashboard endpoint pointed at /webhooks/stripe. Without it that
# endpoint fails closed with a 503 — an endpoint that accepts unsigned bodies is
# an endpoint anybody can post fake revenue to.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Unsplash ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stock photos for a post's featured image, searched from the publishing screen.
# The "Access Key" of an app at https://unsplash.com/oauth/applications — the
# demo tier's 50 requests/hour is plenty for one person picking pictures.
# Unset just hides the picker; uploading your own image still works.
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Writing help (OpenRouter) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subject suggestions, "Clean this up" and sequence drafts in the composer.
# A key from https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys. Give the key a credit limit
# there too. Unset hides every AI button; nothing in core/ai/ is ever called.
OPENROUTER_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Optional. Hard monthly ceiling in US dollars, counted from the ai_calls table.
# AI_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=10
# Optional. OpenRouter model ids per job. Defaults: Sonnet 5 for subjects,
# Opus 5.5 for clean-up and sequence drafts.
# AI_MODEL_SUBJECT=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5
# AI_MODEL_CLEANUP=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5
# AI_MODEL_SEQUENCE=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5
# Optional. Lets Settings → AI store your own OpenRouter, Anthropic or OpenAI
# key, encrypted (AES-GCM). Unset means no key can be saved there. Changing it
# makes every saved key unreadable until it is pasted again.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32. `bun run setup` writes one for you.
# AI_KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET=
# Optional, local only: `fake` answers every helper on this machine, no key needed.
# AI_PROVIDER=fake
